\nweaker outlier predictions. Outdoor enthusiasts, motorists, and\nresidents of recent flood impacted areas are encouraged to remain\nabreast of the developing forecast in the coming days.","ends":"2026-10-29T15:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; San Miguel, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.38c97534038bb54c112c5ff0215b743f983d5cfb.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.38c97534038bb54c112c5ff0215b743f983d5cfb.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-28T23:26:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 282326 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 526 PM MDT Wed Oct 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Mild fall conditions continue through tomorrow. - Increasing precipitation chances arrive Friday morning with light rain and snow above 10000 feet. - Deeper moisture arrives Saturday night and will increase the chances for impactful precipitation for south","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-28T18:10:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-291000- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1210 PM MDT Wed Oct 28 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ign02","station_name":"Ignacio 2","distance_km":16.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f":-999,"soil_temp_15cm_f":-999,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":-999,"wind_speed_mph":-999,"air_temp_f":48.67,"relative_humidity":0.626,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu